## FAQs

### What is a video switcher, and what does MEG's video switcher rental include?

A video switcher cuts a screen cleanly between more than one presentation source instead of forcing a manual cable swap. MEG's real version of this is one Kramer VP-731, a 9 input video scaler and switcher, operated by our technician rather than rented as a self run box. See [The Real Unit We Stock](#the-real-unit-we-stock-one-kramer-vp-731-9-inputs) above for exactly what it is and is not.

### Is this the same as a camera switcher or a live streaming production switcher?

No. This is the single most important distinction on this page. Our Kramer VP-731 switches presentation sources, a laptop, a second laptop, a DVD player, onto your room's own screen. It does not accept camera inputs and it is not built for live streaming or broadcast production. Cameras, filming and live streaming are not in our own inventory either. See [Video Switcher vs Camera Switcher](#video-switcher-vs-camera-switcher-the-question-that-matters-most) above.

### How many sources can it switch between?

The unit has 9 physical inputs, but the honest, typical use case on our real bookings is 2 to 3 sources, a laptop, a second laptop and occasionally a DVD player, not 9 at once. See [What 9 Inputs Actually Means in Practice](#what-9-inputs-actually-means-in-practice) above.

### Can I rent just the switcher without a technician?

No. This is technician operated equipment, so it goes out with a technician, not as a self run box. Consistent with our delivery only model, we also do not offer self collect rentals. On the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/), adding the video switcher requires the on site live technical assistant add on. On the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), the included technician manages it as part of the standard booking.

### Video switcher vs camera or vision mixer for live streaming, what is the real difference?

A video switcher like ours cuts between presentation sources for a room's own screen, a laptop to a laptop to a DVD player. A camera or vision mixer for live streaming accepts multiple camera feeds and produces a program output for a broadcast or a stream to remote viewers, an entirely different category of equipment with a different signal chain. MEG stocks the first. The second, and the cameras, filming and live streaming that go with it, are not in our own inventory. If your event needs a filmed record or a stream to remote attendees, see [Video Switcher vs Camera Switcher](#video-switcher-vs-camera-switcher-the-question-that-matters-most) above.

### Which packages include this, and how much does it cost?

None of our five packages include it as standard. It realistically pairs with the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), which already includes a screen and a technician, or the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) with its technical assistant add on, since this is technician operated equipment. There is no published a la carte price. [Contact us](/contact/) with your package and agenda and we will confirm availability and a quote. See [Which Packages This Is Available On](#which-packages-this-is-available-on-and-pricing) above.

### What sources can it actually switch between?

Confirmed, real sources: a laptop, a second laptop, and a DVD player, drawn from an LG-RH7500 DVD recorder and hard disk unit in our inventory. There is no document camera or visualizer in our own inventory, so neither appears on that list. See [Video Switcher vs Camera Switcher](#video-switcher-vs-camera-switcher-the-question-that-matters-most) above if your event needs one.

### Do you rent the DVD recorder, or other recording equipment, separately from the switcher?

No. The LG-RH7500 DVD recorder and hard disk unit is one of the switcher's three confirmed sources, not a standalone rental item, and it has no camera input. If you are searching for recording equipment rental meaning cameras, lenses or production gear to film your event, none of that is in our own inventory: what we own is audio, screen and lighting equipment for events. See [Video Switcher vs Camera Switcher](#video-switcher-vs-camera-switcher-the-question-that-matters-most) above for how we handle that request.

### Do I need this for a small event, or only for larger corporate bookings?

Only if your event has more than one presentation source on the same screen. A single speaker with one slide deck does not need it, a single laptop connection is genuinely simpler. It becomes relevant on a conference agenda with more than one presenter, or a keynote that includes a video insert, which is why it shows up almost exclusively on our corporate MICE bookings rather than private parties.

### How does this compare to just using one laptop for my presentation?

A single laptop is simpler and needs nothing extra, and it is the right choice if your event genuinely has one presenter and one deck. The difference shows up the moment a second source enters the picture, a second speaker's laptop or a screened video clip. Without the switcher, that source change means unplugging and reconnecting a cable live, with a visible black screen or reboot. With it, our technician cuts between sources with no visible interruption. See [Video Switcher or a Single Presentation Source](#video-switcher-or-a-single-presentation-source-what-changes) above for the full comparison.

### Can I bring my own devices to switch between?

Yes, within the confirmed source types, a laptop or a second laptop connects the same way any presentation laptop does on our packages, through the HDMI and USB-C adapters we already provide. Tell us what devices your event will actually use when you book so our technician can confirm compatibility and the connection setup ahead of time, rather than troubleshoot it live.

### How far in advance should I book this?

Book as early as you can once your event date, venue and agenda are confirmed. See [How Far in Advance to Book](#how-far-in-advance-to-book) above. Because it is a single unit that requires a technician, confirming early matters more here than on equipment we stock in larger quantities.
